Package: lindos-settings
Version: 1.0.0
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, lindos-core, xfce4-settings, xfconf, xdg-utils
Recommends: pavucontrol, xfce4-power-manager, xfce4-notifyd, xfce4-session, mintinstall, mintupdate, mintdrivers, network-manager-gnome, blueman, system-config-printer, gufw, timeshift, mugshot, baobab, lm-sensors, power-profiles-daemon, x11-xserver-utils, lindos-compat, lindos-gaming, lindos-tune
Suggests: lindos-desktop, light-locker-settings, corectrl, openrgb, piper, goverlay, antimicrox, nvidia-settings, synaptic, gnome-disk-utility
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos Settings - Windows-11-style settings centre
 A single settings window for Lindos laid out like
 Windows 11 Settings: Home, System, Personalization, Apps, Windows apps, Gaming,
 Hardware, Network, Accounts, Lindos Mode, Update & Recovery, About.
 .
 Native pages manage the Lindos Mode (Everyday, Gaming, Work, Creator, Lite),
 the RAM meter and quick toggles (Dark mode, Game Mode, MangoHud, compositor),
 theme/accent/wallpaper/taskbar, Windows programs run through Wine/Proton
 (lindos-run, prefixes, recipes, doctor), gaming (Proton-GE, launchers,
 controllers, refresh rate, honest anti-cheat information) and hardware (CPU
 governor, GPU drivers, fans, power profile, RGB, TRIM).  The remaining pages
 delegate to the existing XFCE and system tools to keep memory use low.
 .
 The Apps page lists whatever the Lindos installer could not finish (for
 example while the PC was offline: Google Chrome, drivers, Wine, launchers,
 Flatpak apps), read from /var/lib/lindos/install-state.json, each with an
 "Install now" button that uses the ordinary privileged helper actions.
 .
 "lindos-settings --power-menu" shows the Win+X style power menu.
 The lindos-settings.desktop launcher is shipped by lindos-desktop.
